{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "30", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "18", "M": "54", "S": "13"}}, "news": [{"title": "Plan to develop five cities in state on par with Bengaluru: Karnataka CM", "para": "The government has initiated plans to develop five cities, with Mysuru as one of the key centers, to alleviate traffic congestion in Bengaluru. To facilitate better traffic management, Outer Ring Roads will be established in these cities. This year\u2019s Dasara celebration aims to reach international acclaim, with fresh ideas and increased participation from diverse groups ensuring a grand event.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/plan-to-develop-five-cities-in-state-on-par-with-bengaluru-karnataka-cm/133631214?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-146378/133631214.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Trichy civic body targets top 100 property tax defaulters in city who owe \u20b99.4 crore", "para": "Trichy Corporation is targeting its top 100 property tax defaulters for significant revenue recovery. These defaulters collectively owe the local body Rs9.4 crore in outstanding property taxes. The corporation plans to take strict action against those who continue to delay payments. This includes potential suspension of essential services like water and drainage connections. The move aims to address the ongoing fund crunch affecting city maintenance and new proposals.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/trichy-civic-body-targets-top-100-property-tax-defaulters-in-city-who-owe-9-4-crore/133631181?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-203946/133631181.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Bandlaguda residents urge Telangana government to lift 22-A curbs", "para": "In Bandalguda, the residents of Krishinagar and Ajay Nagar colonies are rallying for the removal of their properties from the 22-A prohibited list. Hundreds of homes, some standing for almost 40 years, were built with proper permits from the authorities. The abrupt classification of their land as government property has thrown their lives into chaos, urging them to seek urgent relief.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/bandlaguda-residents-urge-telangana-government-to-lift-22-a-curbs/133628768?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-211542/133628768.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}